---------------------\nIsambard Kingdom Brunel: A Biography - L. T. C. Rolt - Google Books (https://books.google.com/books?id=gwgZAAAAIAAJ)\nciteturn478search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 67.9 years ago; Crawled: 2 weeks ago; \n\n# Isambard Kingdom Brunel: A Biography\n\nImage: Front CoverL. T. C. RoltSt. Martin's Press, 1959 - Civil engineers - 345 pages By use of private papers hitherto unavailable to biographers, the author reveals the 19th-century England engineer who imparted more momentum to the greatest social revolution in all history than any other single man.\n\n### From inside the book\n\n[Input][Input][Input] [Input]\n\n### Contents\n\nChapter Page I FATHER AND SON  | 3\n | \nORDEAL BY WATER  | 20\n | \n\nTHE YEARS OF FRUSTRATION  | 38\n | \n\n15 other sections not shown\n\n### Other editions - View all\n\n | Isambard Kingdom Brunel: A Biography\nL. T. C. Rolt\nSnippet view - 1957\n | \n\n | Isambard Kingdom Brunel: A Biography. --\nL T C 1910-1974 Rolt\nNo preview available - 2021\n\n### Common terms and phrases\n\nappear arch assistant atmospheric became Benjamin Hawes boilers bridge Bristol Britain broad gauge building built Captain carried Claxton Clifton coach Committee Company completed construction contract cylinder Daniel Gooch diary directors Duke Street Eastern Steam England evidence Exeter experience father floating Gibbs Horsley House hull cite46†I. K. Brunel iron Isambard Brunel Isambard Kingdom Brunel John Scott Russell laid later launch letter Liverpool locomotives London Marc Brunel Marc's Mary Maudslay miles Millwall morning narrow gauge never night once Paddington paddle engines passengers pipe piston proposed pumping rails realised river Robert Stephenson Rotherhithe Russell's Saltash Saunders scheme Scott Russell screw engines seemed shaft ship soon South Devon speed Steam Navigation Steamship Stephenson Swindon Thames Tunnel tide timber tion tons took train viaducts voyage West Western Railway wheels Wootton Bassett wrote yard Yates\n\n### Bibliographic information\n\nTitle  | Isambard Kingdom Brunel: A Biography\nAuthor  | L. T. C. Rolt\nPublisher  | St. Martin's Press, 1959\nLength  | 345 pages--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nIsambard Kingdom Brunel by L.T.C Rolt - Penguin Books Australia (https://www.penguin.com.au/books/isambard-kingdom-brunel-9780140117523)\nciteturn478search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 20.7 years ago; Crawled: 4 months ago; \n\nIsambard Kingdom Brunel\n\nL.T.C Rolt\n\n  * Published: 2 March 2006\n  * ISBN: 9780140117523\n  * Imprint: Penguin Press\n  * Format: Paperback\n  * Pages: 480\n  * RRP: $36.99\n\n# Isambard Kingdom Brunel\n\n  * L.T.C Rolt\n\n* * *\n\nBuy from…\n\nAmazon Booktopia Dymocks QBD Readings Your Bookstore Abbeys Boomerang Find local retailers Collins Fishpond Gleebooks Harry Hartog Kinokuniya Robinsons The Nile Mighty Ape\n\n[Button: View all retailers]\n\n* * *\n\nThe definitive biography of Isambard Kingdom Brunel, one of the greatest figures of the Industrial Revolution and number 2 in the BBC's Great Britons poll.\n\nEngineering genius, technical innovator and one of the greatest figures of the Industrial Revolution, Isambard Kingdom Brunel changed the face of the English landscape with his groundbreaking designs and ingenious constructions. L. T. C. Rolt's masterly biography is the definitive work on Brunel, tracing the life, times and monumental achivements of the man who helped to build modern Britain.\n\n\n  * Published: 2 March 2006\n  * ISBN: 9780140117523\n  * Imprint: Penguin Press\n  * Format: Paperback\n  * Pages: 480\n  * RRP: $36.99\n\nCategories:\n\n  * Biography\n  * Civil engineering, surveying & building\n  * Technology--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBrunel: A Pocket Biography - The History Press (https://thehistorypress.co.uk/publication/brunel-a-pocket-biography/)\nciteturn478search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: 20.6 years ago; Crawled: 3 weeks ago; \n\nImage: Brunel: A Pocket Biography\n\n# Brunel: A Pocket Biography\n\nL T C Rolt,\n\n  * Paperback\n\nRailway 200\n\nBiography & Memoir, History, Transport & Industry\n\nPublication date: 16/03/2006\n\nISBN: 9780750942942\n\nRRP:\n\n£8.99\n\nBuy now\n\n  * Amazon.co.uk\n  * Bookshop.org\n  * Waterstones\n\nAt 19, Isambard Kingdom Brunel was in charge, under his father, of an engineering work that is the wonder of Europe: the Thames tunnel, completed in 1843. This book traces Brunel's life and career, the man of immense energy who came to dominate civil engineering in the 19th century and whose legacy can still be seen nearly two centuries later. L.T.C. Rolt was one of the first narrative historians, an industrial pioneer and preservationist. During his life he was fundamental in establishing and promoting canals, waterways and railways. He was one of the first people in modern Britain to draw attention to the value of our canals as a means of transport and a source of pleasure. As well as his interest in canals he also turned his attention to neglcted railways and set up the first organisation to save and run a railway with a mainly volunteer workforce.\n\n  * About the author\n\n##### L T C Rolt\n\nL T C ROLT was born in Chester on 9 February 1910 and died in 1974. He was an engineer and craftsman, whose passion for Britain’s industrial heritage led him to become one of the foremost historians of the 20th century. He was joint founder of the Inland Waterways Association. He also wrote Narrow Boat, Red for Danger and the famous Landscape Trilogy.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMicrosoft Word - LTCRoltPaper (https://www.ssgreatbritain.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/LTC-Rolt-Life-Work-Legacy.pdf)\nciteturn478search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.0 years ago; \nLegacies of Rolt: Isambard Kingdom Brunel\n\nPaper delivered at ‘L.T.C. ROLT – LIFE, WORK, LEGACY’ - A Joint Ironbridge George Museum Trust & Keele University Conference on 10 MAY 2024\n\nTim Bryan, Director, Brunel Institute\n\nLTC Rolt’s biography of Isambard Kingdom Brunel first published in 1957¹ was not his first book, but the first and arguably the most significant book of a trilogy of highly popular biographies of Victorian engineers that also included George & Robert Stephenson and Thomas Telford².\n\nIn the sixty-seven years since its publication, Rolt’s Brunel book remains in print having appeared in both hardback and paperback under various imprints; in 1989 the book was reissued with a new introduction from Professor Angus Buchanan which provided readers with some context on the book³. The most recent edition dates from 2003 when the book was republished with a new cover to mark Brunel’s appearance in the BBC ‘Great Britons’ TV series the year before; in 2005 Sonia Rolt was keen to see the book once again reissued in hardback in an illustrated format as part of the then forthcoming Brunel 200 celebrations and a letter from her contained in the Rolt archive at Ironbridge noted that the 2003 cover was ‘hated by all’ and ‘much objected to’⁴. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nIsambard Kingdom Brunel : a biography / L.T.C. Rolt | L. T. C. Rolt | London : Longmans, Green (https://www.mwbooks.ie/pages/books/347215/l-t-c-rolt/isambard-kingdom-brunel-a-biography-l-t-c-rolt)\nciteturn478search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 months ago; \n\nImage: Image 1 of 1 for Item #347215 Isambard Kingdom Brunel : a biography / L.T.C. Rolt. L. T. C. Rolt.\n\n# Isambard Kingdom Brunel : a biography / L.T.C. Rolt\n\nRolt, L. T. C. (1910-1974)\n\n1964, Hardback edition. London : Longmans, Green. Fine cloth copy in a near-fine, very slightly edge-nicked and dust-dulled dust-wrapper. Remains particularly well-preserved overall; tight, bright, clean and strong. Item #347215\nPhysical description; 345 pages illustrations 23 cm. Subjects; Civil engineers Great Britain 